The Securities and Futures Commission may conduct inquiries or investigations into suspected violations of the Securities and Futures Ordinance and any subsidiary legislation, codes, and guidelines. 
According to regulations, which enforcement agencies may the Securities and Futures Commission refer serious cases to for further investigation and action? 
I. The Courts; 
II. The Joint Financial Intelligence Unit; 
III. The Independent Commission Against Corruption; 
IV. The Commercial Crime Bureau of the Hong Kong Police Force

The Securities and Futures (Client Securities) Rules apply to which of the following assets (intermediary’s client securities or securities collateral):
I. Securities listed or traded on a recognized stock market; 
II. Stocks received or held in Hong Kong; 
III. Client securities held in a client account opened in the client’s name with an institution other than the intermediary or its associated entity; 
IV. Securities received or held by an authorized financial institution at an overseas branch

The Securities and Futures Commission has issued the "Internal Control Guidelines," requiring all intermediaries to comply.
What is the purpose of these guidelines?
I. To ensure that intermediaries can maintain and enhance their profitability levels; 
II. To ensure that intermediaries safeguard the assets of their clients and the business itself; 
III. To ensure that intermediaries maintain complete records and that the financial and other data used internally and disclosed externally are reliable; 
IV. To ensure that intermediaries comply with all applicable laws and regulatory requirements

Currently, which recognised clearing houses are under Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing Limited? 
I. Central Clearing Company; 
II. The Stock Exchange Option Clearing House; 
III. Hong Kong Futures Clearing Corporation Limited; 
IV. Hong Kong OTC Clearing Limited

The provisions regarding short selling activities under Schedule 11 of the Rules of the Stock Exchange include:
I. Only stocks denominated in Hong Kong dollars are eligible for short selling activities;
II. Exchange Participants must establish a stock borrowing arrangement prior to engaging in short selling to facilitate settlement;
III. Short selling cannot be executed at a price lower than the current best ask price;
IV. Exchange Participants must indicate that an order is a short sale order when transmitting or inputting it

WL Corporation is a large licensed corporation in Hong Kong and an Exchange Participant for options trading on the Stock Exchange. 
To fulfill its clearing functions, the company plans to apply to become a Clearing House Participant. 
According to the relevant regulations of the Stock Exchange, what categories of Clearing House Participant for Stock Exchange Options can the company apply for? 
I. Self-clearing Participant; 
II. Direct Clearing Participant; 
III. General Clearing Participant; 
IV. Independent Clearing Participant.

Under what circumstances can the disclosure of information constitute market misconduct? 
I. Disclosing and widely promoting analysts' reports on companies that may be subject to acquisitions; 
II. Disclosing information regarding prohibited transactions; 
III. Disclosing information concerning suspended trades; 
IV. Disclosing false or misleading data to induce transactions
